                            <comment id="16094764" author="eignatiev" created="Thu, 20 Jul 2017 14:30:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Rerun tests in &quot;Run All&quot; Ignite 2.0 group after merge with the latest master - &lt;a href=&quot;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=734705&amp;amp;tab=queuedBuildOverviewTab&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=734705&amp;amp;tab=queuedBuildOverviewTab&lt;/a&gt; - Do you see any issues with them? (Unfortunately I have too little experience with Ignite tests to judge.)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16094835" author="dpavlov" created="Thu, 20 Jul 2017 15:37:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=eignatiev&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;eignatiev&quot;&gt;eignatiev&lt;/a&gt;, let me check the results for you. I&apos;ll respond to dev list&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16095262" author="cos" created="Thu, 20 Jul 2017 19:56:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Are we tracking the JIRA in two different places? It might create an inconvenience if anyone would ever need to follow through the discussion. It makes sense to keep the JIRA discussion on the ticket (or in the PR &lt;em&gt;if&lt;/em&gt; such PR is named correctly and ASF Infra bot can publish the updates to the JIRA automatically).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16095270" author="dpavlov" created="Thu, 20 Jul 2017 20:01:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=cos&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;cos&quot;&gt;cos&lt;/a&gt;, is my understanding correct that better place to discuss ticket is JIRA/PR comments, but not dev list, for example, thread &lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/IGNITE-5123-Review-td19813.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/IGNITE-5123-Review-td19813.html&lt;/a&gt; ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16095287" author="cos" created="Thu, 20 Jul 2017 20:09:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I am &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; saying one is better than another (and the example you&apos;ve provided doesn&apos;t look that much ticket specific for me, really). I am saying that splitting the discussion through the multiple sources makes it harder for people to use later.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
